        "event": "Special Weather Statement",
        "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued July 16 at 5:09AM AKDT by NWS Juneau AK",
        "description": "|...HIGH WATER CONTINUES ON THE SALMON RIVER...\n\nA glacier dammed lake outburst from Summit Lake continues on the\nSalmon River near Hyder. Water levels as of 5 am Thursday are at\n26.5 ft at the river gage, around 7.5 ft higher then what it\nwas at before the event started. Water levels are expected to\ncontinue to rise with a forecast crest expected by Thursday evening.\nIt is unknown how much water will be released from Summit Lake which\nresults in large uncertainty on exact crest height and timin",
